    "profile_title": "Correct size trigger/hammer+spring tension (mini can print)",
    "profile_notes": "[Plates one and two are for the right-handed, plates 3 and 4 are for the left-handed. A1 mini can print without modification ] The original file had an unrealistically sized trigger and hammer, and the recoil spring was a bit too stiff. I have adjusted the width of the trigger and hammer to match that of an M1911, and I modified the spring tension to be closer to that of a real revolver. This should provide a more realistic dry fire experience. However, I recommend practicing with a real firearm for the best experience, but this version offers a degree of realism compared to the original design. Additionally, I have created another version that further modifies the shape of the trigger and hammer, and added a Picatinny railto more closely resemble those of a real firearm, and it works great, but I worry that some people might use it as a tool for dry fire practice. It’s important to note that grip technique is as crucial as trigger pull when practicing, so I suggest using a more accurate representation for training, so I choose not to upload that version. However, if you are interested in the version with the Picatinny rail, please let me know.",
